fail[3]: A whole word is its own prefix and suffix.
fail[4]: No word starts with "ab" and ends with "z", but "xyz" starts with "x".
fail[5]: "ab" appears at positions 0 and 2, so the answer is 2. No word starts and ends with "b".
fail[6]: 1500 searches, with answers adding up to 2229822. Checking every word for each search takes too long here.
error[TimeoutError]: Checking every word for each search takes too long. In `__init__`, store every prefix and suffix pair of every word in a dictionary, so each search is one look-up.
edges:
- no word fits :: any(c == "f" and not any(w.startswith(a[0]) and w.endswith(a[1]) for w in inputs[0][0]) for c, a in zip(commands, inputs)) :: run(["WordFilter", "f"], [[["abc"]], ["b", "c"]])
- a whole word as both prefix and suffix :: any(c == "f" and a[0] == a[1] and a[0] in inputs[0][0] for c, a in zip(commands, inputs)) :: run(["WordFilter", "f"], [[["abc"]], ["abc", "abc"]])
- several words fit :: any(c == "f" and len([w for w in inputs[0][0] if w.startswith(a[0]) and w.endswith(a[1])]) > 1 for c, a in zip(commands, inputs)) :: run(["WordFilter", "f"], [[["ab", "aab"]], ["a", "b"]])
