fail[3]: "a" goes up to 1 and back to 0, so it's removed, and there are no keys left.
fail[4]: "a" and "b" both end with a count of 1, so both answers are the key that comes first: "a".
fail[5]: "x" is removed, "y" has 2 and "z" has 1.
